FL,385,380,120,260,000,100
PN,38404
SC,0004
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F384A1786553276
OL,3,CA look back at how the South marked
OL,4,Cthe 1999 solar eclipse
OL,6,FDemand for electricity dropped between
OL,7,F11am and 11.30am but as the sun
OL,8,Freappeared from behind the moon, the
OL,9,Fcountry went back to work.
OL,11,FIt resulted in a power surge of 3,000
OL,12,Fmegawatts.
OL,14,FThe peak of this year's solar eclipse
OL,15,Fwill be between 7.05pm and 7.16pm.
OL,17,FThe UK Health Security Agency strongly
OL,18,Fadvises people not to look directly
OL,19,Finto the Sun without safe, industry-
OL,20,Fstandard eclipse glasses, as this can
OL,21,Fseriously damage the eyes.
OL,1,W~s1x0~s1~s hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}   G4/5
